#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi; Basics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi; Databases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many applications such as OpenOffice.org or Microsoft Excel create files "
"which are called <firstterm>documents</firstterm>. &kexi; creates files too, "
"but we refer to them as <firstterm>&kexi; database files</firstterm>, or "
"simple <firstterm>database files</firstterm> here. &kexi; database files "
"usually have the extension <filename>.kexi</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to storing your databases in database files, &kexi; can also use "
"databases on <firstterm>database servers</firstterm>, which is why we refer "
"to them as <emphasis>database files</emphasis>, and not simply as "
"<emphasis>databases</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The term <firstterm>&kexi; project</firstterm>, or simply "
"<firstterm>project</firstterm> is also used to refer to a &kexi; database, "
"regardless of whether it is stored in a file or on a database server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a New Database File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Run &kexi;, or if it is already running, use <menuchoice> <shortcut> "
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose <guilabel>Blank Database</guilabel> and click the <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> to confirm the creation of the project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>New Project Stored in File</guilabel> and proceed with "
"<guibutton>Next</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter a name for your project, and click <guibutton>Next</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the file browser to choose a folder where you would like to save your "
"database file. You may change the file name in the <guilabel>Location:</"
"guilabel> box if you dislike the one that is suggested."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Create</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kexi; Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> and <guilabel>Properties Editor</"
"guilabel> are shown in panes on each side of the child window. These can be "
"resized or hidden as required. A pane can be hidden by clicking the small "
"cross at the top of the pane (just below the toolbar)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Database objects (tables, queries, etc.) listed in the <guilabel>Project "
"Navigator</guilabel> can opened by clicking (or double-clicking, depending "
"upon your global &kde; settings) on their names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main application elements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main elements of &kexi; application's window are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menubar"
msgstr "Barra de menuts"

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"contains available commands for the application. You will find detailed "
"description of any of the commands in the appendix."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbar"
msgstr "Barra d'espleches"

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "contains most frequently used commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel>'s pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"contains a list of any object (tables, queries, forms, ...) created within "
"the currently opened database project. The navigator also contains small "
"toolbar with most usable commands related to the database objects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Opened database objects</guilabel> area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"a central area of the application taking most of the screen space. For IDEAl "
"user interface mode it contains switchable tabs with windows that are always "
"maximized. For Childframe user interface mode it contains floating windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Properties</guilabel> pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"contains a list of properties of currently activated database object. For "
"certain objects (&eg; form's widgets) it can have several tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Taskbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"contains a list of currently opened windows with database objects. For IDEAl "
"user interface mode, it is available as a number of tabs. For Childframe "
"user interface mode, it is available as a number of buttons, behaving just "
"like your operating system's taskbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> pane is one of the most "
"frequently used elements of the &kexi; main window. The pane contains a list "
"of all objects created within the currently opened &kexi; database project. "
"The objects are split into groups: tables, queries, forms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> pane also contains a "
"<emphasis>small toolbar for most frequently used commands</emphasis> (from "
"left to right): <guilabel>Open selected object</guilabel>, <guilabel>Design "
"selected object</guilabel>, <guilabel>Create a new object</guilabel>, and "
"<guilabel>Delete selected object</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each object on the list a context menu is available using the &RMB;. For "
"example, this is context menu for the <emphasis>persons</emphasis> table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double clicking with the &LMB; on the object's name on the list allows to "
"open the object in Data View. If the object's window was alread opened, the "
"action just activates the window without switching it's view mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that your operating system or window manager can be set up to handle "
"single clicks instead of double clicks. In this case it is enough to single "
"click on the object name to open its window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Database object windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening an object's window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the object in the <link linkend=\"project-navigator-pane\">Project "
"Navigator pane</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>Open</guibutton> button on the <link linkend=\"project-"
"navigator-pane-toolbar\">Project Navigator pane's toolbar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands related to object windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "Closing an object window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the IDEAl user interface mode (the default) is used, each window has "
"its own tab. Place the mouse pointer on the icon on the tab. A "
"<guibutton>Close</guibutton> button will become visible. Click it to close "
"the tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the Childframe on the right hand of each opened window there are buttons "
"you can use to control the window. Click the first one on the right hand to "
"close the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, regardless of the user interface mode you are using, you can "
"select <menuchoice><guimenu>Window</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Close</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the Menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Window buttons for Childframe user interface mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other buttons (from right to left) can be used to: maximize, minimize "
"and undock the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There's a small icon on the left side of the title bar which can be clicked "
"to show a context menu with commands related to the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Property Editor</guilabel> pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Property Editor</guilabel> pane you can change properties "
"of the object displayed in the active window. Depending on the context, the "
"pane is consisted of one or more tabs. The first, always visible tab, "
"Properties, contains the list of available properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules for using the Property Editor:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each row contains a single property."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the mouse or the keyboard to change values of particular "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Most frequently used types of property values are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>a number;</emphasis> you can enter the value directly or increase "
"or decrease its value by clicking with the &LMB; on the arrows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "text"
msgstr "tèxt"

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "drop down list of values"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Yes/No;</emphasis> you can toggle the value by clicking on the "
"button; <guibutton>Yes</guibutton> (<emphasis>true</emphasis>) means that "
"the button is toggled on, <guibutton>>No</guibutton> (<emphasis>false</"
"emphasis>) means that the button is toggled off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is no need to confirm a changed value: changes are visible immediately "
"after moving to a different row of the Property Editor's list or by pressing "
"the <keycombo><keycap>Enter</keycap></keycombo> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Names of the recently changed properties that not yet were stored in the "
"database are marked with bold text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After changing the value of a property, a special <guibutton>Undo changes</"
"guibutton> button appears on the right side of the Property Editor's list. "
"By clicking it you can revert the value of the property to the original "
"value that was loaded from the database upon opening the database object. "
"The button is only visible when the property is actually highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Property Editor pane is empty if:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "no single database object's window is opened, or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the active database object's window does not offer properties; it is usually "
"the case when it is opened in Data View instead of Design View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening an existing &kexi; database file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "To open an existing &kexi; database file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "select it in the <guilabel>Open Existing Project</guilabel> dialog; or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "open it by clicking on the .kexi file icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opening a database file in the <guilabel>Open Existing Project</guilabel> "
"dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Run &kexi;. You should see the <guilabel>Choose Project</guilabel> startup "
"dialog. Choose <guilabel>Open Existing Project</guilabel> tab. You will see "
"the following dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From <guilabel>Current location</guilabel> drop down box, pick a folder "
"containing a file you are looking for."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can either pick a file or enter its name in the <guilabel>Location:</"
"guilabel> box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr "Clicatz sus <guibutton>Validar</guibutton>."

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:424 basics.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Nòtas"

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default the <guilabel>Filter:</guilabel> drop down list has "
"<guilabel>Kexi Database File-Based Project</guilabel> selected. In case the "
"file you are looking for has an other extension, you can change the "
"selection of the <guilabel>Filter:</guilabel> drop down list to "
"<guilabel>All Files</guilabel> to display all available files (regardless of "
"an extension)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected a file of an external type, like a MS Access .mdb file, "
"&kexi; will provide you with the option to import the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected a <emphasis>connection data</emphasis> file (with ."
"kexic extension) or a <emphasis>shortcut to a project on database server</"
"emphasis> file (with .kexis extension), &kexi; will display appropriate "
"dialogs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opening an existing &kexi; database file by clicking on .kexi file's icon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click file's icon using your file manager or desktop. &kexi; will open this "
"database project automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Note about database files accessed remotely.</emphasis> You may "
"want to open a database file that is located on a remote source (&eg; a web "
"or FTP server or a MS Windows network share). K Desktop Environment allows "
"you to open files from remote sources directly in applications and to save "
"changes back to the source, but this is not the case with database files. By "
"clicking on a database file located on a remote source, a copy of the file "
"will be downloaded to a temporary directory on your computer and all your "
"changes will be made to this local file. The remote original of the file "
"will remain unchanged, so it's recommended to copy (download) the file to "
"your computer first, then open the file and copy it back to the remote "
"source if you want to make it up to date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using built-in help"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following ways to get built-in help in &kexi; are available:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Handbook in form of electronic document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Handbook is available by pressing <keycombo><keycap>F1</keycap></"
"keycombo> key or selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Help</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>&kexi; Handbook</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "What's This? hints."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>What's This?</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>from the menu bar and click on an area of the "
"application to get hints about it."
msgstr ""
